  "tagline": "Early Java multi-model database mixing documents, graphs and objects, now in patch-only mode.",
  "description": "OrientDB is a Java multi-model database where every record is a document that can also act as a graph vertex or edge, linked by direct physical pointers instead of join tables. It offers an extended SQL dialect with graph traversal, Gremlin support, Lucene-based full-text and spatial indexes, and runs embedded or as a server with Hazelcast-based distribution. SAP acquired OrientDB in 2017 and later wound down commercial support. The 3.2 line still gets regular patch releases (3.2.57 in October 2026), but feature work has moved to forks: its creator's ArcadeDB and JetBrains' YouTrackDB.",
